@Override
@Transactional
public ServiceResult startMedicalHold(String raceId, String bib, StartMedicalHoldRequest request) {
    return withIdempotency(request.requestId(), "START_MEDICAL_HOLD",
            orderedParams(
                    "raceId", raceId,
                    "bib", bib,
                    "holdId", request.holdId(),
                    "medicRole", request.medicRole(),
                    "startedAt", request.startedAt(),
                    "reason", request.reason(),
                    "expectedVersion", request.expectedVersion()),
            () -> {
                // holdId 是第二层全局幂等键：同参重放原结果，异参409。
                MedicalHoldRow existingHold = repository.findHold(request.holdId()).orElse(null);
                if (existingHold != null) {
                    return replayHoldOrConflict(raceId, bib, request, existingHold);
                }
                RaceRow race = requireOpenRace(raceId, request.expectedVersion());
                requireRunner(raceId, bib);
                requireNotDisqualified(raceId, bib, "开始医疗暂停");
                Optional<MedicalHoldRow> active = repository.findActiveHold(raceId, bib);
                if (active.isPresent()) {
                    throw new ConflictException("选手已存在生效中的医疗暂停: " + active.get().holdId());
                }
                bumpVersion(race, request.expectedVersion());
                long now = clock.millis();
                MedicalHoldRow row = new MedicalHoldRow(
                        request.holdId(), raceId, bib, request.medicRole(), request.reason(),
                        request.startedAt(), MedicalHoldStatus.ACTIVE,
                        null, null, null, now, null);
                try {
                    repository.insertHold(row);
                } catch (DuplicateKeyException ex) {
                    MedicalHoldRow concurrent = repository.findHold(request.holdId()).orElseThrow();
                    return replayHoldOrConflict(raceId, bib, request, concurrent);
                }
                MedicalHoldRow saved = repository.findHold(request.holdId()).orElseThrow();
                return ServiceResult.created(ResponseMapper.toHoldResponse(saved));
            });
}

private ServiceResult replayHoldOrConflict(
        String raceId, String bib, StartMedicalHoldRequest request, MedicalHoldRow existing) {
    boolean sameParams = existing.raceId().equals(raceId)
            && existing.bib().equals(bib)
            && existing.medicRole().equals(request.medicRole())
            && existing.startedAt() == request.startedAt()
            && existing.reason().equals(request.reason());
    if (!sameParams) {
        throw new ConflictException("holdId 已用于不同参数的医疗暂停: " + request.holdId());
    }
    return ServiceResult.created(ResponseMapper.toHoldResponse(existing));
}
```

Wait — replay of a hold that has since been RESUMED: returning current state would differ from original response. Hmm. The timingId replay returns the existing row (which is immutable). For holds, the row mutates on resume. If startHold is replayed after resume, returning current row would show RESUMED — wrong replay. But requestId replay (first layer) returns the stored original response — correct. The holdId second-layer replay with a NEW requestId after resume... edge case. To keep evidence stable, I could reconstruct the original response from immutable fields: created response = hold with status ACTIVE, null resume fields. Since those fields are known at creation, reconstruct:

```java
MedicalHoldRow atCreation = new MedicalHoldRow(existing.holdId(), ..., MedicalHoldStatus.ACTIVE, null, null, null, existing.createdAt(), null);
```

